  "summary": "The traditional Sami craft of decorating knives and sheaths with distinctive materials and symbolic ornamentation.",
  "description": "Featuring handles made from reindeer antler, birch, or bone decorated with geometric patterns, pewter inlays, and sometimes silver elements, with sheaths of reindeer leather decorated with similar motifs. These knives evolved from practical tools to objects of status and cultural significance, with ornamentation encoding family identity and social standing.",
